IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`

-- P1-art7: Article 7 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744): amendments to Annex III.
-- The Omnibus did not change Article 7 (the whole Article is the base text in the consolidated text). Article 7 is in Chapter III Section 1, so Article 113 third paragraph, point (c) gives its date:
-- from 2 December 2027 for AI systems classified under Article 6(2) with Annex III. The power to amend Annex III is a power over Annex III, and Annex III is the Annex III route, so the gate passes that route.
-- The Commission's power is not about one AI system, so Article 111(2)'s saving is not in question: the gate is passed the date asked as the placement date (a system placed on the date asked, or later,
-- is never saved) and no significant change (fork F-7-gate). The core's constant for "no AI system in question" cannot be used here: with a placement date of 1 January 1900 the keel would treat the system as placed
-- before Chapter III and saved, and the gate would answer FALSE on every date.
-- Every provision of Article 7 is addressed to the Commission (an official): no seat has a question of its own. A provider meets Article 7 through the seat questions at the end of the provider seat module.
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER. MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE the conditions are met; JUST FALSE the text says in its own words that a condition is not met ("where both of the following conditions are fulfilled", a "where"
-- gate on a power: the periods ruling's rule (b), split site (ii), fork F-7-where); NOTHING not covered (Chapter III has not begun to apply on the date asked).

§ `Article 7(1): adding or modifying use-cases`

-- src:242 | 1. The Commission is empowered to adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 to amend Annex III by adding or modifying use-cases of high-risk AI systems where both of the following conditions are fulfilled:
-- src:243 | (a) the AI systems are intended to be used in any of the areas listed in Annex III;
-- src:244 | (b) the AI systems pose a risk of harm to health and safety, or an adverse impact on fundamental rights, and that risk is equivalent to, or greater than, the risk of harm or of adverse impact posed by the high-risk AI systems already referred to in Annex III.
@ref Art 7(1) the power to add or modify use-cases (src:242-244)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI systems are intended to be used in any of the areas listed in Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI systems pose a risk of harm to health and safety, or an adverse impact on fundamental rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that risk is equivalent to, or greater than, the risk of harm or of adverse impact posed by the high-risk AI systems already referred to in Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 7(1) the Commission may adopt delegated acts adding or modifying use-cases of high-risk AI systems` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the date asked` `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` `the date asked` FALSE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply from 2 December 2027 on the Annex III route (Article 113 third paragraph, point (c)(i))
        OTHERWISE JUST (    `the AI systems are intended to be used in any of the areas listed in Annex III`
                        AND `the AI systems pose a risk of harm to health and safety, or an adverse impact on fundamental rights`
                        AND `that risk is equivalent to, or greater than, the risk of harm or of adverse impact posed by the high-risk AI systems already referred to in Annex III`)
                  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where both of the following conditions are fulfilled" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

§ `Article 7(2): the criteria the Commission takes into account`

DECLARE `Art 7(2) duty` IS ONE OF
    `Art 7(2) take into account the criteria`

-- "the Commission shall take into account the following criteria": eleven criteria (a) to (k), none of them a threshold. The function says whether all of them were taken into account; the rule is a duty with no
-- time limit and no stated consequence, so no trace can show it breached (NOTES.md, rules with no breach path).
-- src:245 | 2. When assessing the condition under paragraph 1, point (b), the Commission shall take into account the following criteria:
-- src:246 | (a) the intended purpose of the AI system;
-- src:247 | (b) the extent to which an AI system has been used or is likely to be used;
-- src:248 | (c) the nature and amount of the data processed and used by the AI system, in particular whether special categories of personal data are processed;
-- src:249 | (d) the extent to which the AI system acts autonomously and the possibility for a human to override a decision or recommendations that may lead to potential harm;
-- src:250 | (e) the extent to which the use of an AI system has already caused harm to health and safety, has had an adverse impact on fundamental rights or has given rise to significant concerns in relation to the likelihood of such harm or adverse impact, as demonstrated, for example, by reports or documented allegations submitted to national competent authorities or by other reports, as appropriate;
-- src:251 | (f) the potential extent of such harm or such adverse impact, in particular in terms of its intensity and its ability to affect multiple persons or to disproportionately affect a particular group of persons;
-- src:252 | (g) the extent to which persons who are potentially harmed or suffer an adverse impact are dependent on the outcome produced with an AI system, in particular because for practical or legal reasons it is not reasonably possible to opt-out from that outcome;
-- src:253 | (h) the extent to which there is an imbalance of power, or the persons who are potentially harmed or suffer an adverse impact are in a vulnerable position in relation to the deployer of an AI system, in particular due to status, authority, knowledge, economic or social circumstances, or age;
-- src:254 | (i) the extent to which the outcome produced involving an AI system is easily corrigible or reversible, taking into account the technical solutions available to correct or reverse it, whereby outcomes having an adverse impact on health, safety or fundamental rights, shall not be considered to be easily corrigible or reversible;
-- src:255 | (j) the magnitude and likelihood of benefit of the deployment of the AI system for individuals, groups, or society at large, including possible improvements in product safety;
-- src:256 | (k) the extent to which existing Union law provides for:
-- src:257 | (i) effective measures of redress in relation to the risks posed by an AI system, with the exclusion of claims for damages;
-- src:258 | (ii) effective measures to prevent or substantially minimise those risks.
@ref Art 7(2) the criteria (src:245-258)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission has taken into account the intended purpose of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has taken into account the extent to which an AI system has been used or is likely to be used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has taken into account the nature and amount of the data processed and used by the AI system, in particular whether special categories of personal data are processed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has taken into account the extent to which the AI system acts autonomously and the possibility for a human to override a decision or recommendations that may lead to potential harm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has taken into account the extent to which the use of an AI system has already caused harm to health and safety, has had an adverse impact on fundamental rights or has given rise to significant concerns in relation to the likelihood of such harm or adverse impact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has taken into account the potential extent of such harm or such adverse impact, in particular in terms of its intensity and its ability to affect multiple persons or to disproportionately affect a particular group of persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has taken into account the extent to which persons who are potentially harmed or suffer an adverse impact are dependent on the outcome produced with an AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has taken into account the extent to which there is an imbalance of power, or the persons who are potentially harmed or suffer an adverse impact are in a vulnerable position in relation to the deployer of an AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has taken into account the extent to which the outcome produced involving an AI system is easily corrigible or reversible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has taken into account the magnitude and likelihood of benefit of the deployment of the AI system for individuals, groups, or society at large` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has taken into account the extent to which existing Union law provides for effective measures of redress and effective measures to prevent or substantially minimise those risks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 7(2) the Commission has taken all the criteria into account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the date asked` `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` `the date asked` FALSE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply from 2 December 2027 on the Annex III route (Article 113 third paragraph, point (c)(i))
        OTHERWISE JUST (    `the Commission has taken into account the intended purpose of the AI system`
                        AND `the Commission has taken into account the extent to which an AI system has been used or is likely to be used`
                        AND `the Commission has taken into account the nature and amount of the data processed and used by the AI system, in particular whether special categories of personal data are processed`
                        AND `the Commission has taken into account the extent to which the AI system acts autonomously and the possibility for a human to override a decision or recommendations that may lead to potential harm`
                        AND `the Commission has taken into account the extent to which the use of an AI system has already caused harm to health and safety, has had an adverse impact on fundamental rights or has given rise to significant concerns in relation to the likelihood of such harm or adverse impact`
                        AND `the Commission has taken into account the potential extent of such harm or such adverse impact, in particular in terms of its intensity and its ability to affect multiple persons or to disproportionately affect a particular group of persons`
                        AND `the Commission has taken into account the extent to which persons who are potentially harmed or suffer an adverse impact are dependent on the outcome produced with an AI system`
                        AND `the Commission has taken into account the extent to which there is an imbalance of power, or the persons who are potentially harmed or suffer an adverse impact are in a vulnerable position in relation to the deployer of an AI system`
                        AND `the Commission has taken into account the extent to which the outcome produced involving an AI system is easily corrigible or reversible`
                        AND `the Commission has taken into account the magnitude and likelihood of benefit of the deployment of the AI system for individuals, groups, or society at large`
                        AND `the Commission has taken into account the extent to which existing Union law provides for effective measures of redress and effective measures to prevent or substantially minimise those risks`)
                  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Commission shall take into account the following criteria" (a criterion not taken into account is the duty unmet)

-- src:245 | 2. When assessing the condition under paragraph 1, point (b), the Commission shall take into account the following criteria:
@ref Art 7(2) the duty (src:245)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 7(2) duty`
`Art 7(2) the duty of the Commission to take the criteria into account` MEANS
    IF `Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the date asked` `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` `the date asked` FALSE
    THEN
        PARTY Operator
        MUST `Art 7(2) take into account the criteria`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Operator BECAUSE "the Commission did not take into account the criteria of Article 7(2) when assessing the condition under paragraph 1, point (b)"
        -- no time limit and no stated consequence (NOTES.md, rules with no breach path); the party is the Commission, an official the core has no constructor for (NEEDS-CORE.md)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

§ `Article 7(3): removing high-risk AI systems from Annex III`

-- src:259 | 3. The Commission is empowered to adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 to amend the list in Annex III by removing high-risk AI systems where both of the following conditions are fulfilled:
-- src:260 | (a) the high-risk AI system concerned no longer poses any significant risks to fundamental rights, health or safety, taking into account the criteria listed in paragraph 2;
-- src:261 | (b) the deletion does not decrease the overall level of protection of health, safety and fundamental rights under Union law.
@ref Art 7(3) the power to remove high-risk AI systems (src:259-261)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the high-risk AI system concerned no longer poses any significant risks to fundamental rights, health or safety, taking into account the criteria listed in paragraph 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deletion does not decrease the overall level of protection of health, safety and fundamental rights under Union law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 7(3) the Commission may adopt delegated acts removing high-risk AI systems from the list in Annex III` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the date asked` `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` `the date asked` FALSE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply from 2 December 2027 on the Annex III route (Article 113 third paragraph, point (c)(i))
        OTHERWISE JUST (    `the high-risk AI system concerned no longer poses any significant risks to fundamental rights, health or safety, taking into account the criteria listed in paragraph 2`
                        AND `the deletion does not decrease the overall level of protection of health, safety and fundamental rights under Union law`)
                  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where both of the following conditions are fulfilled" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
